# Worker CLI Release

When changing the worker CLI, shared build job services, or Firestore data contracts used by the worker:

- Bump `apps/worker_cli_node/package.json` version before publishing.
- Run the worker build/check before release.
- Publish `openci-worker-cli` to npm when the change must reach running workers.
- Remember that running workers check npm `latest` about once per minute, install the newer global package, then exit with the update-requested code.
- The actual restart depends on the host supervisor (systemd, launchd, Docker, etc.); mention this when giving rollout instructions.

For Firestore data contract changes, deploy Functions before relying on worker auto-update.
